Z||000000||Dale||08-19-99||01:03 PM||||What do you guys suggest for timing on an 84 se 4 cyl.  At Idle and just off idle it runs very rough.  Already replaced the TPS, didnt work.  It appears to be jumping the timing way up past max. advance just like a vacuum advance would do.  If I disconect a sensor, the computer goes back to default and the problem goes away.  Any suggestions????<p>Mahalo
Z||000001||Greg Piet||08-24-99||10:27 PM||||in my v6 you need to have the computer set in diagnostic mode to set timing (tidbit of info missing in my Chilton manual)<br>which sensor are yuo disconnecting? (tps?)
Z||000002||Dale||08-25-99||01:39 AM||||Greg<br>It took me a little to figure that one out about the computer but I did quite awhile ago.  I guess memory is good for something every now and then.  It was the MAP sensor that I disconected.  I thought it would be so simple, a problem solved so easily, I went to go get it ( of course they did not have it) it was ordered, I got it, put it in, got bummed out and tried something else.  I still do have the problem.<p>Thanks
